  "content": {
    "Antiarrhythmic drugs are important for managing sinus rhythm and require monitoring for adverse effects and effectiveness. Amiodarone, a commonly used antiarrhythmic, is associated with thyroid abnormalities, pulmonary toxicity, and rarely hepatotoxicity. Pulmonary toxicity can occur in up to 2% of patients, with potentially fatal outcomes. Regular monitoring including chest x-rays and pulmonary function testing might be necessary. Amiodarone may also cause neurological toxicity. Dofetilide, another drug, is associated with torsades de pointes and requires hospitalization for monitoring when initiated. Dronedarone may lead to severe liver injury and requires monitoring for hepatotoxicity. The guideline includes a table with recommended monitoring for patients on amiodarone.": {
      "HYPO OR HYPERTHYROIDISM": "TSH (T3 & T4) at 3-6 months/Every 6 months",
      "HEPATOTOXICITY": "AST/ALT 3-6 months/Every 6 months",
      "QT INTERVAL PROLONGATION": "ECG annually",
      "INTERSTITIAL LUNG DISEASE": "Chest X-ray/Unexplained cough"
    }
  },
